# SR8: the four-card platform replay of the NEW production image: the node agent's serving sequence on all four boards (resolved at run time: none
# named) in a copy of its container running the THIN LAYER image (@THIN_LAYER_IMAGE@: the platform image built on tp4-serve-8 and pre-pulled into the
# rig daemon, given by the manifest-list digest: the daemon uses the containerd image store and a config digest does not resolve). C2_REPLAY_PROFILE
# is the profile the copy must BOOT BY THE IMAGE DEFAULT: the agent forwards no QWEN_C2_PROFILE, so the replay sets none either, and the profile it
# boots here is the one baked into the image's ENV. Each boot's (load, reload, restart) vLLM subprocess log, read from the container (never
# docker logs), must show '[QWEN-C2] profile c2-packed-tp4-8: vLLM argv', the P150x4 mesh line, 'extent block engaged: blocks=2 segments=4,4', the
# request-warm line BEFORE 'packed blocks capture block=0', admission passed with no UNQUALIFIED, parser M armed, 'extent replay engaged' and the
# prefill warm checks; the platform's served name (the :tt alias) must be advertised before and after the restart. Pass: 'PLATFORM_REPLAY passed=True'.
# The replay turns the session cap OFF (THATCH_SERVING_SESSION_CAP=0 in its own environment), so it cannot show the cap: the baked pair was read
# by SB8's provenance, and the cap is read live after the placement (the metrics gauge, eight sessions admitted and a ninth refused).
# The restart step (docker stop with the teardown skipped, then docker start) is the first reopening of the four-card mesh after an unclean exit: a
# wedge there FAILS the replay and blocks the move of :latest; H8 begins with the quad reset and heals.
# Duration (estimate): 45-60 min, then H8's reset. Stop rule: any FAIL stops the window: :latest does not move.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4-seats8 SHIP window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/seats8 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's stop rule, its minutes and the GO rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-8 is the SHIPPING image: the base SB8 builds
# from this branch with the eight-seat profile baked in as its serving default (ENV QWEN_C2_PROFILE) and the platform session cap baked as its
# seat count (ENV THATCH_SERVING_SESSION_CAP). Every job serves that one image, so the bytes that pass are the bytes that ship. Each job still
# names its profile explicitly, so none relies on the baked default. A commit that changes a file the image carries needs a new SB8 build and a
# new tag in every template.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset replay
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-8
C2_PLATFORM_IMAGE=@THIN_LAYER_IMAGE@
C2_REPLAY_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8
